1.1 Introduction to Sets
Asetisacollectionofthings. Thethingsarecalled elementsoftheset. We
are mainly concerned with sets whose elements are mathematical entities,
such as numbers, points, functions, etc.
Asetisoftenexpressedbylistingitselementsbetweencommas,enclosed
by braces. For example, the collection
{
2, 4, 6, 8
}
is a set which has four
elements,thenumbers 2, 4, 6and 8. Somesetshaveinﬁnitelymanyelements.
For example, consider the collection of all integers,
