Example 1.2 Describe the setA =
{
7a + 3b : a, b ∈ Z
}
.
Solution: This set contains all numbers of form7a + 3b, where a and b
are integers. Each such number7a + 3b is an integer, soA contains only
integers. Butwhich integers? If n is any integer, thenn = 7n + 3(−2n), so
n = 7a + 3b where a = n and b = −2n. Therefore n ∈ A. We’ve now shown that
A contains only integers, and also that every integer is an element ofA.
Consequently A = Z.
