Each of these intervals is an inﬁnite set containing inﬁnitely many
numbers as elements. For example, though its length is short, the interval
(0.1, 0.2) contains inﬁnitely many numbers, that is, all numbers between
0.1 and 0.2. It is an unfortunate notational accident that(a, b) can denote
both an open interval on the line and a point on the plane. The diﬀerence
is usually clear from context. In the next section we will see yet another
meaning of(a, b).
