(2, 4), (4, 2)
)
. The following are also ordered pairs:
(
2,
{
1, 2, 3
})
,
(
R, (0, 0)
)
. Any
list of two things enclosed by parentheses is an ordered pair. Now we are
ready to deﬁne the Cartesian product.
Deﬁnition 1.2 The Cartesian productof two setsA and B is another
set, denoted asA × B and deﬁned asA × B =
{
(a, b) : a ∈ A, b ∈ B
}
.
