1.3 Subsets
It can happen that every element of a setA is an element of another setB.
Forexample,eachelementof A =
{
0, 2, 4
}
isalsoanelementof B =
{
0, 1, 2, 3, 4
}
.
When A and B are related this way we say thatA is a subset ofB.
Deﬁnition 1.3 Suppose A and B are sets. If every element ofA is also
an element ofB, then we sayA is asubset of B, and we denote this as
A ⊆ B. We writeA ̸⊆ B if A is nota subset ofB, that is, if it isnottrue that
every element ofA is also an element ofB. Thus A ̸⊆ B means that there
is at least one element ofA that isnot an element ofB.
