11.3 Equivalence Relations
The relation = on the setZ (or on any setA) is reﬂexive, symmetric and
transitive. Therearemanyotherrelationsthatarealsoreﬂexive,symmetric
and transitive. Relations that have all three of these properties occur very
frequently in mathematics and often play quite signiﬁcant roles. (For
